                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "020f7c0d-4ef4-4a57-8721-33d139b877cf",
                        "source_entry_id": "e2d309a2-15f8-3831-a4c3-afe0fd862ac1",
                        "source_sense_id": "ad04d74c-5668-3a09-9eea-6d48a8f0c552",
                        "target_lang_word": "squabble",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "squabble",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "51c8e3ef-c707-3b31-91ec-df98369c17e6",
                                        "entry_id": "29595f59-aa5f-3f4c-b487-42a4a1b6da30",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A minor fight or argument."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7c559046-2967-4b23-a279-328177d489cf",
                                                "sense_id": "51c8e3ef-c707-3b31-91ec-df98369c17e6",
                                                "text": "The children got into a squabble about who should ride in the front of the car."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4bcb1517-1ac0-46e9-9a5f-9b79fe177f63",
                                                "sense_id": "51c8e3ef-c707-3b31-91ec-df98369c17e6",
                                                "text": "It was obvious to the inhabitants of the small coastal town of Bridport that in the midst of these squabbles their need for a railway was going to be overlooked, and they decided to take the matter into their own hands."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d574b837-4043-4840-b9bf-8deab1e587ed",
                                                "sense_id": "51c8e3ef-c707-3b31-91ec-df98369c17e6",
                                                "text": "\"p your mess.\nAlso, as apologetic as you were for occupying my time, which I had hoped to spend with my daughter, you used about twice as many words as you needed to, and wasted an entire paragraph complaining about your colleagues. I went back to the SCP-079 file — Supervisor Valis would have had the thing decommissioned years ago if it weren't for your blatant technofetishism. Yet, you have the gall to characterize the Foundation's ongoing political interventions and military operations as squabbles.\""
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "squabble",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "63eaec59-577a-3940-b3f6-aaa362cce4b5",
                                        "entry_id": "f2bf65eb-7d2b-33b9-983c-e65c7a92f709",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To participate in a minor fight or argument; to quarrel."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a0fb8b4d-f007-496e-8914-ab57a8cf7a75",
                                                "sense_id": "63eaec59-577a-3940-b3f6-aaa362cce4b5",
                                                "text": "The brothers were always squabbling with each other."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8b605129-04c1-428f-892c-d464061fcabe",
                                                "sense_id": "63eaec59-577a-3940-b3f6-aaa362cce4b5",
                                                "text": "The sense of these propositions is very plain and easy, though logicians might perhaps squabble a whole day whether they should rank them under negative or affirmative."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6b815eb7-42e0-3a30-911e-f7fafa876298",
                                        "entry_id": "f2bf65eb-7d2b-33b9-983c-e65c7a92f709",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To disarrange, so that the letters or lines stand awry and require readjustment."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0ad81973-745a-4a6f-81c5-9708c3d9eb59",
                                                "sense_id": "6b815eb7-42e0-3a30-911e-f7fafa876298",
                                                "text": "to squabble type"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "8797fcd6-0e0b-4e62-b9d8-72d2a8a642d7",
                        "source_entry_id": "e2d309a2-15f8-3831-a4c3-afe0fd862ac1",
                        "source_sense_id": "4b5105e7-4817-35ee-9263-63948cf4ba9e",
                        "target_lang_word": "scuffle",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "scuffle",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c9b65293-3bb3-3075-b876-f9c1b3ec3214",
                                        "entry_id": "736b0746-466d-393c-9077-61d62d15c9bb",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A rough, disorderly fight or struggle at close quarters."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6298f3a5-cd50-431b-8e58-9631008596a7",
                                                "sense_id": "c9b65293-3bb3-3075-b876-f9c1b3ec3214",
                                                "text": "The Dog leaps upon the Serpent, and Tears it to Pieces; but in the Scuffle the Cradle happen'd to be Overturn'd: […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "18bdbce0-278c-442b-b84e-936cb0f8a52c",
                                                "sense_id": "c9b65293-3bb3-3075-b876-f9c1b3ec3214",
                                                "text": "It appears the Company had received news that one of their captains had been killed in a scuffle with the natives."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6037da60-d9b8-408a-94ff-467e3740c786",
                                                "sense_id": "c9b65293-3bb3-3075-b876-f9c1b3ec3214",
                                                "text": "Fights ensued as many England supporters attempted to retreat before some stewards moved in. Intermittent scuffles continued to break out until the section of the crowd where the trouble started was vacated."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1e028b53-b55d-33be-8b2d-785f81e5d928",
                                        "entry_id": "736b0746-466d-393c-9077-61d62d15c9bb",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Poverty; struggle."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "slang"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4f6bfb89-07be-4887-884d-af9bb9b25b18",
                                                "sense_id": "1e028b53-b55d-33be-8b2d-785f81e5d928",
                                                "text": "But even on the scuffle / The cleaner's press was in my jeans"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "252257ea-823e-3f1c-afe9-f7e976d4abd4",
                                        "entry_id": "736b0746-466d-393c-9077-61d62d15c9bb",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A child's pinafore or bib."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "scuffle",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7fbc683f-d19c-32fc-b8b6-d0091559e0b5",
                                        "entry_id": "c9273fb7-2666-3959-8bb6-c7946f6880f4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To fight or struggle confusedly at close quarters."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b2250ecb-2484-4d84-93a1-6c9025fe1031",
                                                "sense_id": "7fbc683f-d19c-32fc-b8b6-d0091559e0b5",
                                                "text": "Certainly a gallant man had rather fight to great diſadvantages for number and place in the field in an orderly way, then ſcuffle with an undiſciplined rabble."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c4f3327c-f27e-3c93-8c49-7b4520737bb8",
                                        "entry_id": "c9273fb7-2666-3959-8bb6-c7946f6880f4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To walk with a shuffling gait."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "41d1fd72-e048-4cdc-84ba-c34bc24727e9",
                                                "sense_id": "c4f3327c-f27e-3c93-8c49-7b4520737bb8",
                                                "text": "But shiftings and readjustments ensued, as they are sure to do with a walking-party. Cope presently found himself scuffling through the thin grass and the briery thickets alongside the young business-man."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fd5c6470-db90-3512-ac30-956b12e4d503",
                                        "entry_id": "c9273fb7-2666-3959-8bb6-c7946f6880f4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To make a living with difficulty, getting by on a low income, to struggle financially."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "slang"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c207491a-b3fb-48ef-b6eb-bb880e3e2a86",
                                                "sense_id": "fd5c6470-db90-3512-ac30-956b12e4d503",
                                                "text": "Once a good friend of mine, a fine hoofer who was having trouble getting bookings, ran up to that tree, gave it a big smack, and yelled “Lawd please make me a pimp, any kind of a pimp, long as I’m pimpin’. I’m tired of scufflin’ and my feet are too long outa work.”"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "scuffle",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "15e540ed-a029-3c08-9cdc-a84c6fe880ba",
